  "body": "### Summary\n\nLOT-052 (MPStorage transport, #78, PR #411) relies on stand-in answers for three states that were never captured. Capturing them would confirm what the transport assumes and give each one its own test.\n\n### Captures wanted (operator's accounts only; anonymize per docs/FIXTURES.md)\n\n1. **Storage write answer**: the `bdd.php` POST of the storage thread's first-message edit form (`R60b`), with an unchanged or trivially changed document. Today the transport relies on the ordinary MP edit answer `W15`.\n2. **Storage creation answer**: the `bddpost.php` POST of the new-MP form (`R45b` shape) with `dest=MultiMP` and `sujet=a2bcc09b796b8c6fab77058ff8446c34` (`MPStorage.m:738-767` @ 2440d79), on an account without a storage thread. Today the transport relies on `W10`. This is a write; do it only on a throwaway account or after backing up the document.\n3. **Edit form of a deleted storage message**: GET of the `R60b` URL (`/message.php?config=hfr.inc&cat=prive&post=<post>&numreponse=<n>&page=1&p=1&subcat=0&sondage=0&owntopic=0`) after the storage thread has been deleted, and also by another account. Today the transport reports this case as `posting(.formUnavailable)`; HFR's actual answer is unknown.\n\nAlso open from LOT-052: the answer to the edit POST of another account's message (`R44` form). Nobody has sent it; capture it only if it can be done without changing another member's data.\n\n### Sources\n\n- `docs/lots/LOT-052-mpstorage-transport.md` § Fixtures, \"Pending capture\"\n- `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md` §6c LOT-052, \"Not captured\"\n\n### Acceptance\n\nThe pages are in the corpus with their meta, LOT-052's pending list and HFR-PROTOCOL §6c are updated, and each state has its own test.",
